Peak-family closure currently supports two phases: tetragonal scheelite CaWO₄ accounts for the broad dominant family, while monoclinic room-temperature WO₃ accounts for the sharp triplet near 22.8–24.0° and its higher-angle companions. I see no coherent CaCO₃ or Ca₃WO₆-only family yet; I’ll test both explicitly after the two-phase refinement so overlap cannot hide a real minor component.

